+# T-3691: track levels -5 to +5
+
+Built on tw/levels (from tw/track b19961f2), agent levels, 2026-11-22.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Sim** (`sim/src/track/params.rs`): `MIN_LEVEL`/`MAX_LEVEL` are -5/+5; every table by level is `[f64; LEVELS]`
+  (11) indexed by `level_ix(l)` (from -5), replacing each `(l.clamp(..) + 3) as usize`. The tram tables are named
+  (`TRAM_MULT`, `STREET_TRAM_MULT`); the busway's is the tram one times two thirds as before.
+- **The game's own tools stay within the setting**: `TrackApi::level_reach` (`BASE_REACH` 3, or 5 with the app's
+  setting on, `set_level_reach`) bounds a ramp over or under track (`bridge::ramp_over`'s new `reach`) and a
+  flyover's leg (`flyover.rs` `ramp_levels`, `ramp_leg`). So with the setting off nothing new appears at ±4/±5
+  that the player did not pick; track already at ±5 may still ramp a level toward the ground. Validity (`geom`, `net/edit.rs`) accepts -5..+5 always, so track at the outer
+  levels in a save loads, draws and runs with the setting off. Rebuild to a level (`rebuild_pick`) takes -5..+5.
+- **Saves**: no change. Levels are signed varints read as `i8` (`save.rs` node and PI levels), so -5..+5 already
+  fit; no save level bump.
+- **App**: `Level` is -5..+5, `LEVELS` all eleven top first, `BASE_LEVELS` -3..+3. `pickLevels` (game/ui.ts)
+  is what the level buttons and Settings' Show levels toggles list; `DisplaySettings.allLevels` (off by default)
+  switches it, is sent to the clock worker (`levelReach` message, on change and on each load, as `bindNew` is),
+  and turning it off brings the drawing level back to ±3.
+- **Stroke level packing** (`map/levelCode.ts`, new): a segment's two end heights were 8 bits each at 1/32 level
+  from -4, which only held -4..+3.97. Now 1/16 level from -8 (-8..+7.9), with every decoder (visibility,
+  renderer's sample levels, the stroke shader's colour and hidden-level reads) on the same constants. Shaders'
+  `u_level_colours` are 11 long; the level-hide bits go from -5.
+- Shift+1..7 still set +3..-3; the outer levels have no key, and their hover leaves the key out.
+- Docs: track-and-service.md "Levels", "Ramping over track", construction table, long water, terrain, stations,
+  junction, upkeep. Wiki levels-and-tunnels (table and the roads-per-km figure's indices), station-upgrades (ground
+  index).
+
+## New values (for Anita to check)
+
+| Level | +5 | +4 | -4 | -5 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Track multiplier (rail) | 3.0 | 2.5 | 2.4 | 2.8 |
+| US$M a km, double track | 225 | 187.5 | 180 | 210 |
+| Tram, off street and on street | 2.6 | 2.1 | 2.0 | 2.4 |
+| Station structure part (200 m), US$M | 100 | 85 | 150 | 175 |
+| Station total (200 m), US$M | 150 | 135 | 200 | 225 |
+| Name | High viaduct | High viaduct | Deep tunnel | Deep tunnel |
+| Colour | #e8bcf6 light violet | #c27ce6 light purple | #7a1630 maroon | #8e1a7e dark magenta |
+
+- Steps carried on: up +0.5 a level from +1 (1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0); down +0.4 a level from -2 (1.6, 2.0, 2.4,
+  2.8). Stations +15 a level up, +25 a level down, as before.
+- +3's colour changed for everyone: #4a2c9a (dark indigo) to #9db2fa (periwinkle). CIELAB distance between
+  neighbours: +5/+4 34, +4/+3 37, +3/+2 32, -3/-4 41, -4/-5 42 (the rule is at least 30).
+- Unchanged by level (the obvious continuation): 8 m apart; ramps the same length a level (200 m at 160 km/h,
+  floor 160 m); the ramp speed rule; boarding cost (every level pays the same 2 minutes, T-3910); upkeep (+4/+5 a
+  viaduct's US$50k a km, -4/-5 a bored tunnel's US$130k; stations below ground US$200k); terrain adds at -1 and up
+  (so +4/+5 pay it, -4/-5 do not); long water: +4/+5 are viaducts (30 km limit), -4/-5 bored (no limit).
+- A flying junction's flyover is priced one level away from the ground, toward it from ±3 out, so a ±3 flying
+  junction keeps its old price (the flyover tool at ±3 still goes toward the ground with the setting off).
+
+## Player strings
+
+- New: Settings, Game section checkbox `settingsTab.allLevels` "Use levels −5 to +5" (brief's example was "Show
+  levels -5 to +5"; "Show levels" is already the heading of the level visibility row in Show, so "Use").
+- Changed: `issues.levelRange` "Levels go from −3 to +3." -> "Levels go from −5 to +5." (the refusal for a level
+  out of range, which only an outside edit can now meet).
+- Reused word for word: "High viaduct" for +4/+5, "Deep tunnel" for -4/-5.
+- Changelog levels-1: "added track levels −5 to +5, turned on in settings. +3 track is periwinkle now".
+
+## Layout
+
+Eleven buttons overflowed Settings' Show levels row (the -5 cut off at the dock's edge): its buttons now share the
+row's width (`.level-toggles > .btn.lv` flex). On a phone the level pop-ups (`.tool-bar-pop`, `.blueprint-levels`)
+wrap to two rows. The map's track bar and the selection bar hold eleven at desktop width.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `agent_cargo test` both suites pass (1010 and 788 + the new test). New `ramp_tests::levels_past_three_with_the_setting`:
+  with the setting a +3 route ramps to +4 and a +5 one under to +4; with it off a +5 route still ramps toward the
+  ground; -5 and +5 track priced US$210M and US$225M a km; saved, loaded with the setting off, levels kept, bytes equal.
+- tsc clean; i18n clean (4 stale translations a language, the changed `issues.levelRange` among them).
+- Smoke: first run 2 of 30 failed: t145 (it decoded the old 1/32 packing by hand; now uses `levelOfCode` and checks
+  ±5 fit) and "demand final" timed out at 300 s on 1 core under load. Second run, 3 cores: 30 of 30 passed.
+- `checks/t3157-look.mjs` decoded the old packing and the 7-colour table by hand; brought to the new one, not run.
+- In game (NYC sandbox, port 6130): routes at +5, +4, +3, 0, -3, -4, -5 placed, built, drawn in their colours;
+  setting off: bar shows +3..-3, the drawing level went from +5 to +3, the outer track still draws; Show levels
+  hides +5 then +3 and exactly those routes fade; the selection bar's level buttons show eleven on a blueprint pick.
+  Shot: artifacts/trainworld/review/levels.png.
+
+## Files outside this task's own
+
+- `sim/src/track/cost.rs` (addtrack's): the four table-index sites to `level_ix`, the level table test, three
+  doc comments, and `junction_cost`'s flyover level rule (`BASE_REACH` in place of `MAX_LEVEL`/`MIN_LEVEL`).
+- `app/src/ui/Blueprint.tsx` (addtrack's): its display copies `MULT` and `STATION_M` got the four new levels, and
+  `awayLevel` matches `junction_cost`.
