+# T-3949 Bundles as saved records (track rework stage 2a)
+
+Agent bundles, 2026-11-21, tree `.tw-trees/bundles` (branch tw/bundles from tw/track at ac49304b), Vite 6223.
+Design: notes/T-3444-design/01-model.md, 07-saves.md, 10-build-plan.md (stage 2a). Advisor consulted twice. Before
+the first edit it had me take the parity baseline first, make `LBN1`'s presence (not the level) mark a save from before
+bundles, run the finder after the load's derive and write fields directly, keep one bundle per run, and leave
+`station_beside` alone. Before handing back it found three gaps, all fixed below: `edge_bundles` cost 4.4 ms a state
+read on NYC (now no geometry), doubling up under a line was untested (now tested), and doubling up beside track drawn
+beside laid the new pair on that track (now beside track is bundled, so it is refused as before).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **A bundle on today's edges.** `EdgeData::bundle` (`net::Bundle { id, slot }`, id 0 none), so undo, splits and
+  every copy of an edge carry it: `split_plan` gives both halves the edge's, a joined piece (`unjoin_near`) its first
+  part's, the station-trim piece (links.rs) its edge's. `Network::edge_bundle`, the derived `bundle_members` (live
+  pieces per bundle) and `Network::across(e)` (the pieces of other slots of `e`'s bundle). A set_edge that changes
+  only the bundle sets it and touches nothing, so putting built track in a bundle derives and settles nothing.
+- **Set by drawing quad** (wasm/draw.rs `route_op_as`): every piece of the stroke in one bundle, the drawn pair slot 0
+  and the express pair slot 1; carried on from a loose quad end, that end's bundle with each pair in the slot of the
+  pair it carries on.
+- **Set by doubling up** (wasm/crossings.rs `double_side`): the run and its new pair in one bundle (the run by a
+  bundle-only op per piece, so undo takes it off), the bundle of a loose pair its ends carry on from where there is
+  one.
+- **Set by drawing beside track** (wasm/draw.rs `beside_bundle`, wasm/beside.rs `beside_ends`): the route shares a
+  bundle with the run's pieces between where it starts and ends along the run (their bundle where one has one, the
+  route in the other slot). A piece the route's own edit changes (a start on the run splits it) is left out. Without
+  this, doubling up a double with a double drawn beside it laid the new pair 4 m from that track, on top of it, where
+  the geometry rule refused it; with it, refused as before, and a station on the beside track takes the name of the
+  one beside it, as before.
+- **The geometry finders are gone.** `twin_at` (scanned every edge) is `pair_beside`: the nearest piece of another
+  slot of the bundle within `LEVEL_WITH_M` 15 m (the old rule's outer bound kept as "level with"; no 4 m lower bound,
+  no parallel test), then the old snap to a loose end or joint level with it. `quad_beside` (scanned every node) is
+  `bundle_end_beside`: the nearest loose end at the same level, within 15 m, of a piece in another slot of the bundle
+  of the clicked end. Doubling up's "doubled" (`Alongside`) asks `pair_beside` at a piece's middle; the issue and its
+  string are kept. `quadPairs.ts` and `quadTwin.ts` are deleted: `TrackApi.edge_bundles` (edge, bundle, slot) goes
+  into the rows as `bundle` and `slot`, and the track hover shows 4 strokes on double track where another slot of its
+  bundle has double track. `station_beside`/`on_track_beside` in twin.rs (4-16 m, the hidden twin line's and
+  per-direction stops' rule) are untouched: stage 4 removes them, and changing them moves figures.
+- **The save.** A trailing `LBN1` block after `LBQ1`: count, then per bundle its pieces' count and per piece its edge
+  index and slot, ids renumbered 1 up. Written whenever `Network::bundles_known`, even with no bundles, so its absence
+  alone marks a save from before bundles. A damaged block drops only the bundles (found again), as `LBD1` does. Level
+  **38**: master is at 36 and busways takes 37 there, so 37 is left to it. BLOCKS now 41.
+- **Older saves** (`track/legacy.rs`, load only): `find_bundles` runs once in `TrackWorld::reload` after the derive
+  when the save had no `LBN1`, writing the fields directly. The frozen rule: at each piece's middle, the nearest other
+  piece (crossovers left out) parallel there (sine at most 0.03) 4-15 ground m off. A piece and its find are one
+  bundle in other slots; two such pieces meeting at a two-ended node (a joint, a station) are one in the same slot;
+  union-find with parity, twin links first, and a link that would put a piece in both slots is left out (default quad,
+  whose pairs share their end nodes; a third pair beside a quad gets the first pair's slot, so the nearest of another
+  slot is still the neighbour across). A grid listing each geometry piece in 100 m cells, as a sorted list, makes it
+  cheap. `realsave` sets `bundles_known = false`, so the starts it writes carry bundles found by the rule.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `agent_cargo.py test`: both suites pass (6 new tests in `wasm/bundle_tests.rs`: drawn quad, its station split, save
+  round trip byte for byte, undo; pair beside from the other slot, carried quad one bundle; old saves: two doubles
+  drawn apart are no bundle and stay none, the same bytes without `LBN1` find one and keep it once written, drawn quad
+  through points and default quad survive a save from before bundles; doubling up makes a bundle, undo takes it off,
+  refused a second time, allowed again after the pair's removal; doubling up constructed track under a settled line
+  leaves the line's data, rates and runs identical after the edit and the undo; track drawn beside shares a bundle,
+  refuses doubling up, names its station after the one beside, saves). Seven old tests adjusted only where they
+  assumed the last block written is theirs (`save::bare_end`), plus the level pin (38, 41).
+- `lanes_parity` fingerprints (every path, capacity resource with solved figures, lines' figures) byte identical
+  before and after on Amsterdam test, real NYC, Vienna, North America 383 and the 2,647-station save (scratch
+  `fp.py`; binaries built at ac49304b and after).
+- The finder on those saves (`bundles_found_on_saves`, ignored; `T3949_NETS`): Amsterdam 842 pieces, 24 bundles
+  holding 60, 3 ms; NYC 1,647, 75 holding 624, 16 ms; Vienna 4,058, 196 holding 560, 33 ms; NA 5,940, 20 holding 289,
+  38-42 ms; Tokyo 8,590, 19 holding 313, 46-48 ms. The grid finds exactly what scanning every piece finds (asserted
+  there; the scan took 0.2-28 s). The first grid (a map of 50 m cells) took 200 ms on NA and was replaced.
+- Native load (`lanes_parity` "load or build", two runs each, base / after, ms): Amsterdam 19-25 / 25, NYC 100-108 /
+  117-124, Vienna 515-531 / 467-495, NA 292-309 / 339-344, Tokyo 431-435 / 437-465: at most about 1.15x, within part
+  8's 1.2x for stage 2. A save written by this build skips the finder.
+- `edge_bundles` per state read: first with the piece beside each middle, 4.4 ms on NYC and 2.2 on Tokyo, too much
+  for every read; now ids and slots only.
+- `agent_cargo.py wasm`, `npm run check` clean.
+- In the browser on Vite 6223 (3 cores), before the last two fixes (beside bundling, rows without geometry): the real
+  save 12,886,431 rail trips a day, 109 lines; 628 pieces in 75 bundles; the hover on the LIRR's Port Washington
+  branch shows the 4-track icon (`../artifacts/trainworld/t3949-quad-hover.png`). The reference saves load and
+  calculate: Amsterdam test 252,040 rail trips a day, 45 lines; Vienna 1,569,738, 43 lines; NA 383 27,199,321, 134
+  lines (no browser baseline exists for these; their lines' figures are the native fingerprints above, and demand
+  reads nothing of bundles). `t3333-pairs.mjs` and `t3348-perdir.mjs` PASSED.
+- After the last fixes, on the final build: both suites 731 + 950; the real save again 12,886,431 rail trips a day,
+  109 lines, 628 pieces in 75 bundles in its rows; smoke (`TW_CORES_WANT=4`) 29 of 30, 222 s, the one failure "wiki
+  figures" (below, not this task's).
+
+## For landing (orchestrator)
+
+- DECISIONS line (the main tree's file refused my edit; landing's):
+  - 2026-11-21 (agent bundles, T-3949, on tw/track, advisor consulted): quad's pairs are a saved bundle (an id and
+    slot per edge, `LBN1`, save level 39, after master's `LBO1` at 38), set by drawing quad, doubling up and
+    drawing beside track (with the run's pieces it lies along). The block is written whenever the bundles are known,
+    even with none, so its absence alone marks a save from before bundles, which finds them once on load by the old
+    twin rule (frozen in `legacy.rs`, pieces of a pair meeting at a joint or station joined into one bundle);
+    `realsave` writes none, so the starts find theirs too. The pair beside a point is the nearest piece of another
+    slot of its bundle within 15 m (the old rule's outer bound, kept as "level with"), with no lower bound or
+    parallel test. notes/T-3949.md
+- Merged onto tw/track 924b642c (master's busways at level 37 and `LBO1` at level 38): `LBN1` is level 39, after `LBO1`
+  in `BLOCKS` and in the encode/decode order, and the app's `SAVE_LEVEL` reads 39. A master level-38 save (no `LBN1`) loads and
+  finds its bundles by the old rule (`checks/fixtures/t4018-busway-only.save`).
+- `git rm` staged the deletion of `app/src/map/quadPairs.ts` and `quadTwin.ts`; nothing else is staged.
+- No player text changed; no changelog item (the rework's is written at its release). The hover's 4-track icon now
+  follows bundles: on old saves the old rule's finds (4-15 m, parallel within 1.7 degrees) where quadPairs took
+  5-11 m within 18 degrees, and a double drawn beside a double at 12 m now counts 4.
+- Smoke's one failure, "wiki figures": `wiki/read/brt.md` is out of date on the branch base (its source changed in
+  c5f02902 without a rebuild); `python trainworld/tools/wiki_build.py` fixes it. Not this task's.
+
+## Left for later stages
+
+- 2b reads `bundle`/`slot` for the shared pointer pick and replaces Double up with the Select bar's 4.
+- 3b's converter reads `LBN1` bundles for quad (07-saves step 3 now says so).
