+# T-3951 Every track its own edge: the compile (track rework stage 3a1)
+
+Agent trackedges, 2026-11-21, tree `.tw-trees/trackedges` (branch tw/trackedges from tw/track a7818245). Design:
+notes/T-3444-design/01-model.md "The derived graph", 05-sim.md sections 1-2, 08-performance.md "The compile, per
+bundle", 10-build-plan.md row 3a1. Advisor consulted twice. Before the first edit it set the shape: paths stay in
+piece terms, the compile owns tracks, ids, places and moves behind accessors, `TrackId` a newtype, ids checked
+against four rules (unrelated edits, loads, undo, today's key order), a per-node track-end list in place of the
+`u8` masks, the way rule kept as the track way's filler. Before handing back it asked for a rerun of the suites on
+the final source, a fallback for an entry no track runs, a test of the ids, the two deviations below stated
+plainly, and these notes' corrections (12 m, the A B A B layout, the seam's staleness line).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **The compile** (`sim/src/track/compile.rs`, new). Each piece (today's edge) is compiled as a bundle of its
+  tracks: per track a `TrackId`, its piece, its way (`WAY_AB`, `WAY_BA` or both) and its offset from the centre
+  line (4 m apart, `TRACK_PITCH_M`; double track -2/+2 m by running side, single 0). Per node, `NodeTracks`: every
+  track end with its place across the node in metres, whether trains arrive and leave on it, and the moves as a list
+  of (arriving track end, leaving track end); a port mask view (`to`) for callers that walk piece ends. Built in
+  `derive` after the ways: `compile_piece` for every touched piece and every piece whose way changed, then
+  `compile_node` for their nodes. The compile's own tables take any number of tracks (`layout` lays n as doubles side
+  by side, A B A B, an odd last one both ways; `NodeTracks` holds any number of track ends), but nothing makes a
+  piece of more than two yet: `set_edge` refuses other counts, and `track_of` and the port masks assume one track
+  each way (the seam, below). Three or more is unexercised.
+- **Ids**: a block per piece id (at least two ids), taken the first time the piece is compiled and kept while it
+  lives, dies and comes back (undo), replaced only if the piece needs more tracks than its block. Within a block the
+  track running a to b comes first. A load compiles pieces in order, so ids come out as `2 * piece + (0 for a to b)`:
+  exactly the old `edge * 2 + dir` capacity keys, and an unrelated edit keeps every other id. `TrackId` is a newtype
+  so it can't index a piece's arrays by mistake.
+- **Node pitch**: piece ends on one side sit in rank order, neighbours half their widths plus 4 m apart (`END_GAP_M`;
+  two doubles 8 m as before, a single beside a double 6 m, two singles 4 m, a future 4-track end beside a double
+  12 m so their tracks never interleave). Replaces `rank * PORT_PITCH_M`. Only the order of places is read (every
+  crossing test is a sign test), so nothing moved.
+- **Capacity's keys** (`capacity.rs`): a track section's key is the track a path entry runs on (`track_of`);
+  "directed" is a property of the track (it runs one way); a key's piece is `track(k).piece` (was `k / 2`), the
+  incremental pass marks the tracks of hot pieces (was `e * 2`, `e * 2 + 1`); `track_edges` takes the network.
+  `Resource.edge` stays a piece id. Junction crossings read the node's move places (`node_move_places`).
+- **Gone**: `lanes.rs`'s `Lane`, `Lanes` (the two-lane cap), `Network::lanes`, `lane_of`, `Moves`,
+  `derive_moves`, `Network::node_moves`, `PORT_PITCH_M`, `LANE_HALF_M`. `moves_after`, `move_ok`, `move_at`,
+  `node_unusable`, `ends_in` and the `UNUSABLE_*`, `WAY_*` constants now live in `compile.rs` and read the compile.
+  `dir_ok` is `track_of(p).is_some()`. One-way single track is asked of the compile (`one_way_single`) in
+  `perdir.rs`, `back_lines` (paths.rs), `rebuild.rs` and `node_unusable`.
+- **The way rule stays, renamed** (`lanes.rs` -> `ways.rs`, `git mv`): `edge_way`, `derive_ways`, `run_group`,
+  `group_ways`, `join_away`, `join_applies`, `flip_reversals`, `pin_station_runs`, `join_for`. It is now only the
+  filler of a single track's way, which the compile reads (deviation below).
+- Tests: `lanes_tests.rs`'s first three rewritten on the compile (tracks by running side and ids in piece order;
+  the move table equal to the old rank rule as moves and as crossing pairs, not as absolute positions; routing reads
+  the table, through a test-only `drop_moves`). Two capacity tests read keys through `track(..).piece`.
+- Docs: code-map.md (track files), track-and-service.md (the "Lanes" paragraph is now "Tracks", the way rule's file),
+  world.md (running side). No player text, no app change.
+
+## Two deviations from the plan row
+
+**No authored track or join record yet.** Row 3a1 opens with "authored bundles with tracks, nodes with joins". The
+compile reads today's `EdgeData` (its track count, `oneway`, `join`) and the running side; there is no stored
+per-track record with an id, way or partner, and joins are still the 2-valued `EdgeData::join`. Storing tracks as
+records belongs with the save that holds them (3b's TWT7); until then a piece's tracks are fully determined by those
+fields, so a record would be a second copy to keep in step. For 3a2: partners have nowhere to be stored but the
+compile's `Track` (derived on every compile, from the piece: on double track each track's partner is the other one
+of its piece), unless 3a2 adds the field to `EdgeData` itself.
+
+**The inferred-way code stays (for 3f).** 10-build-plan.md row 3a1 says "lanes' cap and the inferred-way code out"; 05-sim.md's stage table and 08-performance
+put `derive_ways`, `run_group`, `group_ways` under 3f ("way spreading with reroutes"). Deleting the rule now needs
+three things outside 3a1: a saved marker telling old saves from new (3b's TWT7), tools that set a way when they draw
+(3e/3f: a single off a double's end takes the way of the track under the pointer), and removing the track panel's
+"Use automatic way" (player text, none expected here). So the rule stays as the one filler of a single track's way
+(`ways.rs`, its header says 3f replaces it), and only the compile turns that into tracks. Advisor's default; 3f
+deletes it.
+
+## Where the seam is (for 3a2 and 3c)
+
+Still in piece terms: `LineData::path`, `Run::segs` and every keyframe, profile, boarding and demand entry
+(`edge << 1 | dir`); `turns_back`, `turn_end`, `port_side`; platform resources (`(station node, side_in)`, stations
+are nodes); `Resource.edge`; the app's rows. A piece has at most one track each way until paths are track spans
+(3c), so `track_of` is exact and the port masks (`NodeTracks::to`, `moves_after`) are a lossless view of the move
+list; a piece of 3 or more tracks would need 3c's spans first. Joins (`edge_join`) still only feed the way rule, as
+before: the compile connects a track end to every track end on the other side whose way fits (01-model's rule for an
+unjoined end); joins by track id that restrict moves are 3e's.
+
+- `dir_ok`, `track_of` and the moves now read compiled state, which is stale between a raw setter (`set_edge`) and
+  the next `derive`; before, `lanes()` read the piece's fields live. Nothing in the suites asks in between.
+- Ids equal `2 * piece + (0 for a to b)` only where blocks were first compiled in piece order (every load); a piece id
+  reused in a session keeps its old block, and a new id past the end takes the next block, so in-session ids stay
+  in piece order unless an id was handed out and never compiled.
+- An entry against its piece's way (no track runs it) takes the piece's first track as its capacity key, as the old
+  key named the piece whatever; a running line should never have one.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `agent_cargo.py test` on the final source: both suites pass, 738 + 959 (one new test,
+  `t3951_track_ids_stay_put`: an edit elsewhere keeps every piece's ids, delete and undo gives a piece its own back,
+  single made double keeps its block).
+- `lanes_parity` fingerprints, base (a7818245) against the final source, both built on the agent profile: **byte identical**
+  on `game`, `game-left`, `mirror-right`, `mirror-left`, Amsterdam test, Vienna, real NYC and North America 383
+  (every path and return path, reroutes, 600 station pairs, badges, junction inspectors, guard pairs, every capacity
+  resource with users and solved figures, lines' figures, stop chainages). So 3a2 starts at zero difference on the
+  derived keys; what it adds (partners, turn moves) is new. Scratch: `fp.py`, `cut_track.py`'s cuts, `fp/` outputs
+  in this agent's scratchpad.
+- Native timings, one run each, base / after (ms): load NYC 113 / 104, Amsterdam 27 / 21, Vienna 439 / 419, NA 315 /
+  326; 600 station pairs NYC 1.2 / 1.3, NA 4.6 / 5.2, Vienna 69 / 74; station split on NYC's busiest edge 1.0 / 0.9;
+  stop click NYC 2.7 / 2.7. Within noise; the compile runs inside the load's derive.
+- `agent_cargo.py wasm` and `npm run check` clean on the final source. Smoke (`SMOKE_PORT=6172 TW_CORES_WANT=4`)
+  on the final state 30 of 30, 214 s (and 30 of 30 before the last two edits); the real save 13,252,828 rail trips a
+  day, 109 lines, both runs.
+
+## For landing (orchestrator)
+
+- DECISIONS line: 2026-11-21 (agent trackedges, T-3951, on tw/track, advisor consulted): the compile
+  (`compile.rs`) gives each piece's tracks ids from a block per piece id (at least two, a to b first, kept across
+  death and undo, numbered in piece order on load, so they equal the old `edge * 2 + dir` keys), places track ends
+  across a node half the two ends' widths plus 4 m apart, and holds each node's moves per track end; capacity keys
+  sections by track. Line paths stay `(piece, dir)` until 3c. Two departures from row 3a1: tracks are still read from
+  `EdgeData` (count, `oneway`, `join`) with no stored track record until 3b's save, and the way single track takes
+  from its joins stays as the only filler of a track's way (`ways.rs`) until 3f, since deleting it needs 3b's save
+  marker, 3e/3f's tools and removing "Use automatic way". notes/T-3951.md
+- `git mv` staged `sim/src/track/lanes.rs` -> `ways.rs`; `compile.rs` and this note are new, unstaged.
+- No player text changed; no changelog item.
