+# T-3953 New save format and old saves (track rework stage 3b)
+
+Agent tracksave, 2026-11-21, tree `.tw-trees/tracksave` (branch tw/tracksave from tw/track 9d1fa229), Vite 6176.
+Design: notes/T-3444-design/07-saves.md, 01-model.md, 10-build-plan.md row 3b. Advisor consulted before the layout
+(it set the rule below: TWT7 is an exact image of what the model holds now, one bundle per piece in piece order, so
+track ids and every fingerprint stay put; named the four places 07-saves taken literally would break that; asked for
+the frame field, the old-build test and the three-way parity) and before handing back.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **TWT7** (`save.rs`, level **40**, app `SAVE_LEVEL` 40). The same 20 bytes as TWT6 (magic, origin), then varints:
+  body level (`BODY_LEVEL` 1, its own counter: a higher one is refused as `NEWER_FORMAT` before anything is read),
+  frame (`FrameKind`, so one format covers every frame), running side. Then:
+  - nodes: position, level, flags (bit 0 flying; bit 1 "joins of its own", never written yet);
+  - stations naming their node (node delta, flags built / off / named / one-track way, upgrades, platform, name);
+  - line sets (for "Only for {lines}"): count, 0 for now;
+  - bundles, one per piece in piece order: node deltas, flags (built, off, thru, crossover, sep, `TrackKind` in 3
+    bits, single track's two joins as held), track count, then **per track one varint: way (bits 0-1), purpose
+    (2-3), an offset profile flag (4), partner slot + 1 above (0 none)**, from the left looking a to b; PIs and
+    drawn-through points as TWT6's;
+  - lines and every trailing block exactly as TWT6's (shared code), `LBN1` included.
+  The track list is general (Anita's call relayed 11-21: tracks held one by one, any count, each with its own way
+  and partner or none, no pairing assumed); this build writes what pieces hold (1 or 2 tracks, the double's ways by
+  running side, partners each other) and counts anything else as unread (purpose, an offset profile, a way or
+  partner other than its piece's, a node's joins, a line set, more than two tracks), so the game refuses such a save
+  as newer rather than lose it.
+- **Old saves convert on load**: `read_old_body` reads TWT4-6 into today's records (the old decoder, unchanged), the
+  rest of the decode is shared, and the next save writes TWT7. `encode_old` (test only) writes the old body for the
+  converter's tests. `is_old_model`, `is_newer_magic` now past `7`.
+- **App**: `isOldTrackModel`; `openSave` returns `"frame" | "model" | false`; a slot in TWT6 is written again at once
+  and its old bytes kept under **`old-model-<slot>`**, written only if none is there yet (the first original stays),
+  deleted with the slot and swept like `old-frame-`. A file or a real network's start converts and keeps nothing.
+  `trackFrameKind` reads TWT7's frame field (without it every TWT7 load would read "equirect" and convert again);
+  `isNewerTrackFormat` past `7`; the save check and the shared-save check accept `TWT[4-7]`.
+- `lanes_parity --resave <file>`: saves what loaded, asserts it writes back to the same bytes after a reload, and
+  fingerprints the reload.
+- Docs: architecture.md section 11 (format, newer rule, "The old track model"), world.md (frame), code-map.md.
+
+## Departures from 07-saves (all because the model cannot hold them yet; each stage that can, adds it)
+
+1. **Quad is not one bundle of four.** A piece holds at most two tracks until paths are track spans (3c), and one
+   shared alignment would change the pairs' lengths. Each piece is its own bundle record; `LBN1` still groups pieces.
+2. **The inferred way is not baked.** Way 0 ("the way its run takes by itself") is a file value, so "Use automatic
+   way" and later edits behave as before; it is the marker 3f asked for when it deletes the rule.
+3. **Joins stay per piece end** (the 2-bit left/right as held). Track end to track end on the node is 3e's; the
+   node flag for it is reserved.
+4. **Paths stay `(piece, dir)`**, including the broken line's "none" entry (T-2820); spans are 3c's, at the same
+   body level.
+5. **Partners are written, not held in memory.** Brief said "the compile reads the stored record instead of deriving
+   partners". Not done: a single's partner follows a way that is still inferred and changes with edits elsewhere, so
+   a stored copy would go stale, and a double's has one possible value until tools can lay other pairings. The file
+   carries each track's partner; the decoder checks it against the piece's and counts a mismatch as unread. The
+   in-memory record lands with the first tool that sets a partner (Add a track, AA/BB).
+6. Stations are a section of their own right after the nodes (07 puts them after the bundles): at 3b they name a
+   node, and the decoder sets every station before any piece, as the old one did.
+
+Not done here: `pipeline/readsave.py` (reads TWT4-6; `realauto.py`'s `keep` and service reads take a save given
+to them, which a player's game now writes as TWT7) and shonei-server's save check (`twVerdictNew` for TWT7, stores without checking; must walk TWT7 when
+tw/track merges into master). Both filed below.
+
+## Checks
+
+- `agent_cargo.py test` on the final source: both suites pass, 742 + 963 (two new tests:
+  `save::tests::old_saves_convert_to_twt7_and_twt7_round_trips`: every frame and running side, a network of every
+  piece and station field; the old bytes convert to exactly what TWT7 writes and back without loss, TWT7 reads whole
+  and writes the same bytes; `fields_for_later_stages_count_as_unread`: purpose, a double's way, a node's joins).
+  `tests.rs` `a_newer_network_format_is_refused_as_newer`: stage 1's rule copied as shipped (`> b'6'`) refuses this
+  build's bytes and passes `encode_old`'s; TWT8+ and a body level above 1 are `NEWER_FORMAT`. Eight tests whose
+  assert named the written magic now name TWT7's frame (`twt7_frame`).
+- **Parity**, `lanes_parity` (agent profile), against 3a2's final fingerprints (trackparity's `fp/after2-*`), three
+  ways: this build on the old bytes (which `lanes_parity` passes through `convert_save_frame`, so the old body is
+  decoded and the load reads the TWT7 it gives), the same loaded and re-saved (`--resave`), and that TWT7 file loaded
+  on its own: **byte identical** on Amsterdam test, real NYC, Vienna and North America 383, and on `game`, `game-left`,
+  `mirror-right` (re-saved). `mirror-left` re-saved differs only in `-0.0` against `0.0` in 3 node positions (its
+  mirrored x of 0 is -0.0, which any save writes as 0, the old format too). Every re-save wrote back to the same
+  bytes after its reload. Scratch: `fp.py`, `fp/` in this agent's scratchpad.
+- Master's level-38 fixture (`checks/fixtures/t4018-busway-only.save`, TWT6, no `LBN1`): identical all three ways;
+  its TWT7 carries `LBN1`, so the finder runs once.
+- Native load, ms (one run): base / old bytes / TWT7: Amsterdam 20 / 23 / 24, NYC 100 / 107 / 88, Vienna 426 / 464 /
+  402, NA 302 / 310 / 268.
+- `agent_cargo.py wasm`, `npm run check` clean.
+- In the browser (Vite 6176): a slot seeded with the Amsterdam test save (TWT6) and opened at start loads converted
+  (46 lines), the slot then holds TWT7 and `old-model-<slot>` holds the original bytes exactly; opened again it
+  converts nothing and the kept copy is unchanged; no page errors (scratch `convcheck.mjs`; its "slot written again"
+  wait on the slot's `at` failed, cause not checked; the TWT7 bytes in the slot and the exact kept copy show the
+  write). That load reads TWT6 straight into `TrackApi.load` (no frame conversion). The real NYC save (TWT4, frame
+  and model converted): **12,886,431 rail trips a day, 109 lines**, as master. Amsterdam test through `play.mjs`
+  (3 cores): 246,516 rail trips a day, 45 lines, the same on this tree's base (9d1fa229, stashed and rebuilt);
+  T-3949's 252,040 was an earlier branch state.
+- Smoke (`TW_CORES_WANT=4`, against Vite 6176): SMOKE PASSED, 30 checks, 322 s; its real-save final 13,252,828 rail
+  trips a day, 109 lines, as in 3a1 and 3a2's smoke.
+
+## For landing (orchestrator)
+
+- DECISIONS line: 2026-11-21 (agent tracksave, T-3953, on tw/track, advisor consulted): saves are TWT7 at level 40,
+  an exact image of today's model: a body level of its own (1), the frame as a field, nodes, stations naming their
+  node, line sets, one bundle per piece holding each track one by one (way, purpose, offset profile, partner or
+  none, any count), then TWT6's lines and blocks; fields the model cannot hold yet are written absent and read as
+  unread. Old saves (TWT4-6) convert on load and the slot keeps its first original under `old-model-<slot>`. Quad as
+  one bundle, baked ways, node joins, spans and an in-memory partner wait for the stages whose model holds them.
+  notes/T-3953.md
+- Shared files with trackdraw (3d): none of its files. Touched: `sim/src/track/save.rs` and six test files' magic
+  asserts, `sim/src/bin/lanes_parity.rs`, `app/src/workers/{saveFile,slots,clock.worker}.ts`,
+  `app/src/game/sharedSave.ts`, three docs. 3c (spans) will change the lines section at the same body level.
+- **Level hazard**: tw/track is at 40 now; master's next level must be renumbered past it at the next merge.
+- No player text; no changelog item.
+
+## Filed (not done)
+
+- `pipeline/readsave.py` learns TWT7 (with 3g, when the starts are written in it).
+- shonei-server's save check walks TWT7 and levels 39-40 before tw/track merges into master.
+- 07-saves.md's level table still says "TWT7 body level 36" for 3b-3c; the body level is its own counter, 1 here
+  (the design agent updating the docs may fold it in).
