+# T-3954 Line paths in track spans (track rework stage 3c)
+
+Agent trackpaths, 2026-11-21, tree `.tw-trees/trackpaths` (branch tw/trackpaths from tw/track 641d9154), Vite 6175.
+Design: notes/T-3444-design/05-sim.md section 6, 01-model.md "Line", 10-build-plan.md row 3c; her 11-21 call in
+notes/T-4023.md (tracks are N singles; the partner is only the default for the return run). Advisor consulted before
+the layout (it set: paths stay `(piece, dir)` entries in memory with one typed seam, since `TrackId` is a derived id
+that must not go into lines, ops, undo or the save; the kept return is an input carried by undo, not a derive cache;
+`back_lines`' "beside" half stays; ops in the same edit for exact undo; body level 2 with level 1 still read) and
+before handing back.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Return by partner lookup** (`perdir.rs`): `partner_back` maps the forward path backward entry by entry onto each
+  track's partner (`Network::partner_entry`, compile.rs: the partner track, the other way, where it runs that way),
+  with today's stop-fit rules; `routed_back` routes where it fails. `back_run_of` is the two in turn, worked out
+  afresh (candidates, stretches). On today's pieces the lookup is exactly the old `p ^ 1` test
+  (`t3954_partner_is_reverse`, both running sides, two-way and one-way single).
+- **Routed returns kept** (`Network::line_back: Vec<Option<RoutedBack>>`, net.rs): only where the lookup fails and
+  a route is found. A line's own return is `back_run(l)`: the kept one while it still runs (`kept_back`: live track,
+  its ways, a move or turn between entries), else worked out as before, so a kept return an edit broke never reads
+  the line as broken before `back_ops` replaces it (a sketch, `way_reroutes`). `back_path(l)`, `check_line` and
+  `build_run` for the whole plan read it. Set by a new `Op::Back`; `Op::Line`'s inverse, and `Op::DeleteEdge`'s for
+  a line it reroutes, carry a kept return the op cleared, so undo, redo and rollbacks put back exactly what was
+  there. `set_line` clears it when the plan (stops, path, ones)
+  changes or the line goes. Its touch is `Touch::backs` (rebuilt and checked for broken, not checked as a line the
+  player set: through `t.lines` a kept return changing made edits that leave a line broken refuse).
+- **When a kept return is routed again**: `TrackWorld::back_ops`, last step of `apply_rerouted` on checked edits
+  (after `way_reroutes` and `twin_ops`): the lines the edit set, those on touched pieces, those stopping at touched
+  stations, and `back_watch`'s. New track elsewhere never moves it. A load routes them once where the save has none
+  (`Network::keep_backs` in `reload`); the running-side flip clears them all first.
+- **`back_lines` is gone**, replaced by `Network::back_watch(edges)`: lines keeping a return over the touched
+  pieces; lines with no partner somewhere that keep none (no way back found, or a loop run one way by its track,
+  T-3835), looked for again after every edit; and lines stopping beside a one-way platform (`way_beside`), which stay
+  rebuilt every edit because `way_stops` picks by distance until stage 4 stores picks. Used by `derive`'s broken
+  flags, `lines_touched`, `way_reroutes` and `oneway_plan`. So a line whose return goes round one-way track is no
+  longer rebuilt (service, departures) on every edit anywhere.
+- **Spans** (compile.rs): `TrackSpan { piece, slot, dir }` and `span_slot` (the slot TWT7 gives the track running
+  that way: single track's one track, double's right one a to b with right-hand running), `Network::span_of` and
+  `TrackSpan::entry_of` as the one crossing. In memory paths stay entries.
+- **Save, TWT7 body level 2** (`save.rs`, `BODY_LEVEL` 2; header `LEVEL` stays 40, the app's `SAVE_LEVEL` too: an
+  older tw/track build refuses body level 2 as `NEWER_FORMAT`): each path entry as before plus its track's slot + 1
+  (0 on a dead piece, T-2820's none), then per line 0, or 1 and its kept return (stops as node deltas, path as
+  spans). A slot other than `span_slot`'s is counted unread (refused as newer rather than lost). Body level 1 TWT7
+  and TWT4-6 read as before and route returns on load. `convert_frame` copies kept returns.
+- `lanes_parity` prints `kept returns N` to stderr.
+- Docs: track-and-service.md (the T-3094 way back, T-3348's rebuild note, T-3835), architecture.md section 11 (body
+  level 2), code-map.md (`partner_entry`, `span_of`).
+
+## Departures from row 3c (advisor's call, for the orchestrator)
+
+1. **Paths are not spans in memory.** `LineData::path`, `line_path` and every consumer keep `edge << 1 | dir`
+   entries. `TrackId` is the compile's derived id (re-blocked when a piece outgrows its block), so it cannot sit in
+   lines, ops, undo or the save, and an authored slot held in memory goes stale on a running-side flip while single
+   ways are still inferred (3f). The save writes spans; `span_of`/`entry_of` are the seam. **A piece of more than two
+   tracks (6a, T-4024 Add a track) still waits**: it needs paths held as spans with a compiled entry list.
+2. **Routing still searches `(piece, dir)` states** (`find_path_side`, `loop_back`), not track ends. With one track
+   each way per piece the two are the same graph; converting it now is risk without a case, and T-3952's first-stop
+   turn cause is still unconfirmed. Goes with 1.
+3. **`back_lines`' "beside" half stays** as `way_beside`, for stage 4 (stored stop picks).
+
+## Checks
+
+- `agent_cargo.py test` on the final source: 744 + 965, all pass. New: `t3954_partner_is_reverse`,
+  `t3954_kept_return_stays_until_its_track_is_touched` (kept on set and running; far track leaves it and
+  `back_watch` skips the line; the decoded save holds it before any load routes one, and a reload writes the same
+  bytes; a split of the leg under it, sketched, leaves it not running and the line not broken; a station split into
+  that leg as an edit routes it again in the edit; undo puts back path and kept return exactly). No test of
+  `Op::DeleteEdge`'s inverse with a kept return. Changed: `tests.rs`
+  `a_partly_built_one_way_loop_arc_is_one_of_back_lines` renamed `..._is_watched_for_its_way_back`, asserting
+  `back_watch(&[])` (it keeps no return: a loop run one way). The t3565 tests (`oneleg_tests.rs`, 7) and
+  `perdir_tests.rs` pass; there is no t3565 browser check.
+- **Parity** (`lanes_parity`, agent profile; base built from this tree's untouched source and checked identical to
+  3b's `conv-*`; scratch `fp.py`, `fp/` in this agent's scratchpad folder `trackpaths`): this build on the old bytes
+  **byte identical** on game, game-left, mirror-right, mirror-left, Amsterdam test, Vienna, real NYC, North America
+  383 and the t4018 fixture (gates A and B). Re-saved as body level 2 and loaded again (`--resave`): identical on all
+  but mirror-left's known `-0.0` (as in 3b); every re-save wrote back to the same bytes; the TWT7 files loaded alone
+  equal 3b's `seven-*`; 3b's body level 1 files (`tracksave/fp/*.twt7`) loaded by this build equal them too. Kept
+  returns, all running: Vienna 31, Amsterdam 8, each game 2, NYC and NA 0.
+- Native timings, base / after (ms): load Vienna 503 / 482, NYC 120 / 122, NA 350 / 331, Amsterdam 23 / 26 (one run
+  each, noise). Vienna's stop click, three runs each on the final build: edit 97-123 / 74-80, undo 91-113 / 52-57,
+  likely its 31 lines keeping returns no longer rebuilt and re-placed on every edit (not traced). NYC's, which keeps
+  none, 4.6 / 3.1 in one run: noise.
+- `agent_cargo.py wasm`, `npm run check` clean. `t3348-perdir.mjs` on Vite 6175: PASSED (9 of 9).
+- Smoke, the perdir check and the NYC load ran before the last fix (kept returns that stop running count for
+  nothing; `Op::DeleteEdge`'s inverse); NYC keeps no returns, the perdir case none either.
+- Smoke (`TW_CORES_WANT=3`, against Vite 6175): SMOKE PASSED, 30 checks, 302 s; its real-save final 13,252,828 rail
+  trips a day, 109 lines, as in 3a1, 3a2 and 3b's smoke.
+- The real NYC save in game (`play.mjs` on Vite 6175, 3 cores): **12,886,431 rail trips a day, 109 lines**, as
+  master and 3a2/3b.
+
+## For landing (orchestrator)
+
+- DECISIONS line: 2026-11-21 (agent trackpaths, T-3954, on tw/track, advisor consulted): a line's return run is the
+  partner lookup (each track's partner, the other way), and where that fails the route found is kept with the line
+  (`line_back`, TWT7 body level 2, `Op::Back` so undo is exact), routed again only when an edit sets the line,
+  touches a stop of it or a piece either run uses; lines with no way back, and lines beside a one-way platform
+  (stage 4), are still looked at after every edit. Paths stay `(piece, dir)` entries in memory and in routing; the
+  save names each entry's track slot (`TrackSpan`). Paths as spans in memory and routing on track ends wait for a
+  piece of more than two tracks (6a). Fingerprints byte identical on gates A and B. notes/T-3954.md
+- Shared files with trackdraw (3d): none of its files (`wasm/snapshot.rs`'s `line_back_path` calls `back_path`,
+  unchanged in signature). Touched: `sim/src/track/{compile,perdir,net,service,world,save,tests}.rs`,
+  `sim/src/track/net/{paths,validate,derive,edit,store}.rs`, `sim/src/track/wasm/{oneway,lanes_tests}.rs`,
+  `sim/src/bin/lanes_parity.rs`, three docs.
+- No player text; no changelog item.
+
+## Filed (not done)
+
+- Paths as spans in memory, routing on track ends: with 6a / T-4024 (a piece of more than two tracks).
+- `way_beside` goes with stage 4's stored stop picks.
+- `pipeline/readsave.py` reads TWT4-6 only, and shonei-server's save check does not walk TWT7 (3b's filings): both
+  now also need body level 2's slot varint per path entry and the kept return per line.
+- Loops: `runs_once` and `back_laps` still route a line's own return afresh, so whether a loop runs one way by its
+  track can drift from the return it keeps (a loop keeps none while it runs once; the case is a loop that keeps one
+  and then new track elsewhere changes the fresh answer). Small, no stage named yet.
