+# T-3955 Draw each track at its own offset (track rework stage 3d)
+
+Agent trackdraw, 2026-11-21, tree `.tw-trees/trackdraw` (branch tw/trackdraw from tw/track 9d1fa229), Vite 6178.
+Design: notes/T-3444-design/01-model.md ("Lateral offset", "Node", the stand-ins table), 08-performance.md (3d's
+no-regress guard; stage 5 is where the lane split goes), 10-build-plan.md row 3d. Advisor consulted before settling
+the rows and before handing back ("Advisor", below).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **The sim says where each track is drawn** (`sim/src/track/drawn.rs`, new; `Network::drawn_tracks`). Every track at
+  its own offset from its piece's centre line (`Track::off`), and at each end the offset where it meets the tracks it
+  connects to across the node, decided from the compile's moves and the end's join, in this order:
+  - join: single track whose end has a join that counts meets the double's track the join names;
+  - one-way leg: one-way single track at a junction (3+ ends) with no join meets the one track its moves reach on the
+    piece across the node it runs most nearly straight into; if that piece is single track (T-3209), it stays on its
+    line;
+  - merge: double (or more) track whose tracks connect across the node only to single track that was not moved onto
+    one of its tracks meets that single track's line (today's automatic merge, which old saves keep until 3e);
+  - single lead: a two-way single moved onto one track whose moves also reach the double's other track gets a lead.
+  Ends are drawn at the node's point; `TrackEnd::pos` (rank spacing) is never used for drawing. Nodes with no single
+  track are skipped. Read through the compile's accessors only: no field added to `Track`, `EdgeData` or the save.
+- **Per-track rows to the app**: `TrackApi::track_rows` (`wasm/snapshot.rs`): the track count, then per live track
+  id, piece, way, offset, partner, drawn offset at a and at b; then the leads (node, piece, end, from offset, to
+  offset, the single's piece, so a lead is faded unless both pieces are built). `StateRows.edges` groups the tracks of
+  pieces not drawn as default into `ClockEdge.offsets` (per track: offset, at a, at b; compared for row reuse) and
+  keeps the leads for `ClockState.leads`.
+- **The drawing reads them** (`app/src/map/network.ts`): `trackPoints` draws each track at its offset, easing at an
+  end to where the sim says it meets the node: single track smoothly over `EASE_M` 80 m (on a piece shorter than
+  that, from one end's offset to the other's over the whole piece, so a short piece joined at both ends never dips),
+  held off the tracks leaving that node beside it on the side it moves away from for up to 300 m (T-3120's hold,
+  `heldAt`; the neighbours come from the drawing, but only for ends the sim moved); the tracks of a piece of more
+  evenly over `TAPER_M` 40 m (half the piece at most). One track is drawn shifted off the centre line; two as one
+  stroke at their middle with their gap as `Strokes.lane` (renderer and shaders unchanged; a symmetric narrowing keeps
+  the old single cut point, so zoomed out it looks as before); a piece of three or more (none can exist yet) draws
+  each further track as its own stroke. Where single track splits at a station (T-3212, drawn by the app until stage
+  7) the double keeps its tracks apart there. The edge cache keys on the offsets and the hold's neighbours.
+- **Gone**: `legShifts`, `shiftedEnds`, `LegShift`, `joinSign`, the taper (`taperAt`, `lanePoints`, `joinedAt`,
+  `singleAt`, `doublesAt`) and `singleLeadStrokes` (now `leadStrokes`, drawing the sim's leads with the same look).
+  The ghost's joined ends (`joinedGhost`, tools.ts) use `trackPoints`; the ghost's own taper (T-3171) stays in
+  tools.ts as it was.
+- Docs: track-and-service.md (new "Where tracks are drawn" under "Track settings"; the join bullet and the
+  single-lead line point to it), ui-map.md ("Each track at its own offset" replaces "One-way legs from their own
+  track"; single-lead crossovers from the sim), ui-building.md (the ease and the narrowing), code-map.md (`drawn.rs`).
+  Wiki: new page `tracks` ("Tracks"), its line in index.md, rebuilt.
+
+## Anita's quad call (orchestrator's message mid-task), partly met
+
+"Quad is just N single tracks side by side ... draw each track at its own offset from its own place across the
+piece, with no assumption that tracks come in doubles or that a piece has at most 4."
+- Rows and `trackPoints` are per track and take any count.
+- Two tracks of one piece are still drawn as one lane stroke (their middle and gap): exact for any two offsets, but a
+  gap over 4 m is drawn at 4 m (`Strokes.lane` tops out at 255). Stage 9's spreads, or wider spacing, need per-track
+  strokes, which 08-performance puts at stage 5. A stopgap, not the call met.
+- Three or more draw as separate strokes; that path has never run (no piece can have them yet).
+- The sim's join rule still names a double's outer track (2-valued `EdgeData::join`) until 3e's joins by track id;
+  the merge rule says "double or more".
+
+## The look (screenshots)
+
