+## Part A: ways spread, tracks traced (closes T-3662)
+
+- **A way spreads to the branch points** (`spread_ways`, wasm/oneway.rs; `Network::track_trace`, ways.rs): a way set
+  on a piece of single track (one way, reverse, both ways, automatic) is set on every piece of its segment out to the
+  nearest branch points: through nodes where just two pieces with as many tracks meet, stations included, never into a
+  crossover. Pieces walked b to a take the way turned. A piece the player asked for keeps its own way; of two spreading
+  onto one piece, the first asked wins. One edit, one undo; the lines' confirmation names every line the whole
+  segment moves (`oneway_effects_many` takes the same spread). The rule is in the sim, not the app, so any caller
+  (`set_edges_oneway`) gets it.
+- **No quiet breaks** (`way_lines`): a line the way change keeps on its path must still pass every line check in the
+  edit's sketch (`check_route`), else the edit is refused naming it ("{line} has no other way between its
+  stations.", reused). T-3662's lines broke this way: the path still ran, but a one-way station's place among the stops
+  no longer held (a station on a leg made half two-way stops being a one-way stop).
+- **The notice** (`oneWay.spread`): when the edit went past the pieces picked, "Set one way for 1.7 km, out to the
+  junctions." (reverse: "Reversed 1.7 km of track, ..."; both ways: "Set both ways for ..."; automatic: "Set the
+  automatic way for ..."). `oneway_reach` gives the pieces.
+- **Tracing one track** (`TrackApi::trace_track`, `traceTrack` in game/blueprintPick.ts, `traceAt` in
+  map/trackPick.ts): a double click on track that was already the pick there (its whole, or one track of it) traces
+  the track under the pointer out to the branch points both ways, one track of each double piece (single track: its
+  pieces). From any other pick a double click picks the run of whole track, as before (T-1680). Decided by the pick
+  before the double click's first click (both click paths keep it: `noteClick`, the tool's `onUp`), so nothing waits
+  on a timer. Plain selecting gets track double clicks too (main.ts; before, only trains). Shift+click on track past
+  a traced (or one) track adds the trace of the track under the pointer there.
+- **One track named by its slot** (map/trackPick.ts `OneTrack { edge, slot }`, slot from the left looking a to b,
+  TWT7's order); its way is `trackDir` (game/oneTrack.ts). The pick holds `tracks` (one or a trace) where it held
+  `track`. Remove on a trace removes that track on every piece in one edit (`TrackApi::delete_tracks`, op
+  `deleteTracks`), refused naming the line as for one. The panel for a traced track sums length, levels and slowest
+  curve over its pieces; the map highlights the track on each piece.
