+- **The starts are rebuilt by re-saving, not by a pipeline rerun** (a departure from 07-saves "rebuilt by the pipeline,
+  not converted"; reason below). `realsave --resave <in> <out>` loads a start's network bytes as the game does
+  (`TrackApi::load`) and saves them (`TrackApi::save`), refusing bytes that do not write back the same after a
+  reload. `realnet.py resave [city ...]` runs it on every shipped start (`data/packs/real/<id>.save`, read only) and
+  wraps the result with the original TWG1 header byte for byte into `$REALNET_OUT/<city>_real.save`, which
+  `realnet.py ship` then copies in. Reusable at stage 4f if that stage's converter keeps parity.
+- **`realsave --shared` lays bundles from the pipeline** instead of the load's geometry guess: `realshared.py` marks
+  each edge it laid side by side (`beside`: [group, place across]; a piece's pairs `p<piece>`, a station's platform
+  tracks `s<group>`), and realsave joins them with the finder's own run rule, now shared:
+  `legacy::find_bundles` = old-rule pairs into `legacy::lay_bundles(net, links)`, which realsave calls with the
+  pipeline's links (adjacent places across in other slots, the same place in one). `bundles_known` is set, so the
+  save carries `LBN1` and a load finds nothing. A track per line (no `--shared`) keeps the finder.
