+# T-3959 Stations as platform records (track rework stage 4a1)
+
+Agent trackplat, 2026-11-22, tree `.tw-trees/trackplat` (branch tw/trackplat, cut from tw/track e9c63fce, moved
+onto 4a6d8be6 (3e) before the final checks; the uncommitted work popped back with no conflict), Vite 6185.
+Design: notes/T-3444-design/01-model.md ("Platform", "Stop point", "Station"), 02-station.md, 05-sim.md (sections 2
+and 4, the parity gates), 07-saves.md, 10-build-plan.md row 4a1. Advisor consulted once before any edit (it set the
+departure and the order below) and once before handing back.
+
+## The departure
+
+Row 4a1 says "stations stop splitting track". Taken literally, a platform would lie mid-piece and the compile would
+cut the piece into derived edges at its stop point. Pieces *are* the derived edges today (compile.rs header; 3c's
+departure 1: paths stay `edge << 1 | dir` in memory), every consumer indexes piece arrays, and the parity gate is
+fingerprints keyed on piece and node ids. So in this stage:
+- the records and their ownership move: stations and platforms are records of their own, the station fields on the
+  node are gone, and stop points come from the platforms;
+- each stop node stays a real node in the piece graph (07-saves step 6's fallback: "the node stays as a plain joint
+  and the platform runs across it"), and nothing is merged across it. Merging (only where lengths match to the bit)
+  stays 4b's, as 07-saves gives it. Placing a station still splits a piece at a node (the station tool is 3e's
+  draw.rs, untouched).
+T-4024 (Add a track) and 4a2 (smart allocation) need stop points per (station, track); `stop_point` gives them, and
+4a2 has a place in the save to store its picks.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Records** (`net.rs`, `net/stations.rs`). `Station` (name, named, built, off, upgrades, berth, day, fare, own,
+  road) in `Network::stations` by id, and `Platform` (station, length, `along`: beside the track that carries trains
+  along the node's axis, `one_for_travel`, or against it) in `Network::platforms` by id. In this stage a station's id
+  is its node's, and its platforms' ids are `2 * station` (along) and `2 * station + 1` (against): stable, numbered
+  in node order on load, kept across delete and undo by construction. The twelve `node_platform`, `node_name`, ...
+  `node_road` arrays are gone.
+- **What each old field became**: platform length -> each platform's `len`; `one` -> which platforms exist (0 both,
+  1 only along, 2 only against; `station_one` reads it back); on single track one platform is today's "trains can't
+  pass here" (`no_passing`) and two are the drawn passing loop; the running-side flip swaps a one-track station's
+  platform (`flip_one`). Ports' berths and BRT stations' roads stay on the station record, keyed by their node (both
+  sit on no track; the design never placed them, so they keep their node as anchor).
+- **The node-keyed boundary kept**: `StationData`, `station_data(n)`, `set_station(n, ..)`, `Op::Station` and every
+  wasm call are an adapter over the records, so undo, the edit tools, `realsave` and the app are unchanged. Reads go
+  through accessors (`platform_len`, `station_built`, `station_name`, `station_upgrades`, `station_one`, ...), about
+  400 sites rewritten by a script (`trackplat/accessors.py` in this session's scratchpad); writes go through
+  `station_mut` (save's day, fare and own name blocks, name tidying).
+- **Stop points** (`stops.rs`, new): `stop_point(n, side_in)`: the platform a train arriving at node `n` from that
+  side stops at, with its capacity key (0 on one constructed track, else the side); None where no platform serves its
+  track (a one-track station's other track). `platform_tracks(n)`: the tracks a station's platforms serve. Capacity's
+  platform resources (through stops and a circle's first stop), the turn places (`ceil(p / 2)`, all `p` with a
+  terminal, `p` the platform tracks: 05-sim's formula, which equals today's on every case) and `run_passes` read
+  them. Key values and sort order are today's. Derived on each ask from the two platform records, not kept in the
+  compile: they change in an edit before the next derive, and callers such as `perdir` ask in between.
+- **Save: TWT7 body level 3, header level 41** (app `SAVE_LEVEL` 41; master is at 38). Stations lose their platform
+  length and one-track way; after them a platforms section: per platform its station (delta among the stations),
+  flags (bit 0 against the axis; bits 1-3 reserved, each a field after the flags: 1 its place on its track as bundle,
+  slot and start chainage in mm, 2 a width in cm, 3 its faces), length. Per line stop one varint for its stored out
+  and back stop points, 0 (none stored) until 4a2. Anything set in a reserved field, two platforms beside one track,
+  two lengths at one station, or a station with none is counted unread (the game refuses the save as newer). Body
+  levels 1 and 2 and TWT4-6 read as before through the same `set_station`, so old saves convert on load.
+  `pipeline/readsave.py` reads body level 3.
+- Docs: architecture.md section 11, code-map.md (`stations.rs`, `stops.rs`), track `mod.rs` list.
+
+## Departures, for the orchestrator
+
+1. Stations still split pieces (above).
+2. A platform names its track by the node's axis, not by track id or slot: exact while a node has at most one track
+   each way. A piece of 3+ tracks (T-4024, 6a) needs a slot there (the flag bits reserve the place for it).
+3. A platform's place is its station's node; 07-saves' (start track, chainage, length) waits for the stage where a
+   platform leaves its node (4b's merging or 4d), in the reserved flag bit 1.
+4. Station ids are node ids; the node-indexed blocks (`LNK1`, `LOR1`, `LFR3`, `LFZ1`, `LSN1`, `LBT1`, `LBD1`) stay
+   node-indexed, where 07 expected station indexes. They change when ids part (4b's twin merging).
+5. `stop_point` is derived per ask, not compiled into `dg`.
+6. compile.rs untouched but for two accessor swaps (`platform_len`).
