+## What changed
+
+- **Stored picks** (`LineData::picks`, `Network::line_picks`): per stop station, the station a run that cannot stop
+  at its own platform (a one-way station's, or a one-track station's on the other track) stops at instead, at most
+  one each way. Keyed by station like `ones` and `only`, so they survive reordering, `straighten`, stretches and
+  `best_slot`'s tries. `tidy_picks` (in `set_line`) keeps them to the line's stops, drops a pick naming a stop of
+  the line (T-3605: two listed stations are two stops) and any on a one-way stop the player set (T-3711).
+- **Reading them** (`perdir.rs`): `way_stops` is `way_runs` with a lookup of the stored pick serving the run's way
+  (`pick_for`), where today it called `way_station`; a one-way station's other run now asks too (before, legs were
+  skipped). Threaded with the line's picks into the line-level callers only: the service's runs (`build_run`,
+  `build_on`), `check_route`, the stretch, `runs_once`/`back_laps`, `back_to_keep`, `back_run`
+  (`back_run_with`). Hypothetical routes during an edit (`legs.rs` ordering, `settle_ones`' scoring, the way
+  reroutes, wasm/oneway.rs) keep `back_run_of` with no picks: they ask whether a way back exists, which a pick never
+  changes (the back pick of a one-way station is the listed station's own run).
+- **Making them** (`settle_picks` in wasm/lines.rs, beside `settle_ones` at every stop edit, and in
+  `set_line_with_trains`): a stop the click made (new to the line, an end now between the ends, a one-way stop the
+  player set now served both ways) gets one by smart allocation (`smart_picks`: `way_station` with one-way stations
+  admitted, nearest of the complex then within 300 m, serving that way, no stop of the line and no other stop's
+  pick); every other stop keeps what it has. So her split: clicking either leg's station takes the other leg's for
+  the other way, a two-way stop in one click; clicking both lists two stops each served once (T-3605); dropping one
+  never pairs the other again.
+- **Shift click on a one-way station** (`one_way_stop`): not on the line, it is added with no pick (served one way,
+  as before 4a2); on the line, its pick is dropped (one way) or made again (both ways). The hover rows are T-3711's,
+  unchanged (a one-way station served once shows no shift row, as before).
