+# T-4031 Track records on pieces (track rework stage a)
+
+Agent trackmodel, 2026-11-22, tree `.tw-trees/trackrec` (branch tw/trackrec from tw/track fdaf5bc2). Plan:
+notes/T-4030.md stage a. Advisor consulted before the first edit (below).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **`sim/src/track/tracks.rs`** (new): `Tracks` (a piece's tracks in slot order, from the left looking a to b),
+  `TrackRec { key, way, partner, join: [Join; 2] }` and `Join { Auto, Left, Right, Loose }`. `Tracks::valid` is what
+  the model holds now: one or two tracks with unique keys; a single with the player's way (0-3) and no stored
+  partner; a double with no way set (the running side gives its ways), each track the other's partner, joins only
+  `Auto` or `Loose`. Helpers: `new(n)`, `single(way, join)`, `single_way`, `single_join`, `set_way`, `set_join`,
+  `loose_at`, `cleared_at(end)` (a split's new joint), `reversed()` (a piece seen from its other end: slots
+  reversed, ways turned, join ends swapped; a join's side is seen looking out from its node, so it stays),
+  `keep_one(key, way)`.
+- **The records replace the fields**: `EdgeData::tracks` is a `Tracks` (was `u8`), and `oneway`/`join` are gone;
+  `Network::edge_recs` replaces `edge_oneway` and `edge_join`; `edge_tracks` stays as the count, written only by
+  `set_edge`. Reads through `oneway_of(e)` and `end_join(c)` (ways.rs). `set_edge` refuses records `valid` refuses.
+- **The compile reads them** (`compile_piece`): each `Track` gets its record's `key`, a double's partner from its
+  record, a single's from its way (which may still be inferred), and `loose` per end. `layout` returns each track's
+  slot so ids map to records.
+- **`Join::Loose`**, the one new capability: a track end that connects to nothing across its node. `compile_node`
+  makes no move through the node from or to it; the node's turn moves stay (a station's turnbacks and a bare end's
+  turn to its partner stand for crossovers not yet drawn, stage 8, and the route search tests a first-stop turn by
+  side, so the two still agree). The way rule takes a loose single end as saying nothing (`Vote::None`);
+  `join_away`, `drawn.rs` and the app's `join_edges` see it as unjoined; `set_way` never overwrites it.
+- **Each site that builds records** (carry or reset, the advisor's list):
+  - split (`split_plan_in`): both halves carry the records, the new joint's ends `Auto`;
+  - joining pieces across a joint (`unjoin_near`): compares count and way only (not keys or joins); the joined
+    piece keeps its own records with its outer pieces' far-end joins, slot by slot along it; a joint where any track
+    ends loose is never joined away;
+  - delete one track (`track_delete_plan`): the kept track keeps its key and joins (`keep_one`);
+  - flyover legs: a single keeps its record, a double's becomes one new track; the leg itself `Tracks::single`;
+  - single to double and back (rebuild.rs), station trims (links.rs), new track (draw.rs, crossings.rs): new
+    default records, as they reset way and joins before;
+  - the two raw writes (`pin_station_runs`, `flip_right_hand`) set the single's way on its record.
+  - `rebuild.rs`'s "free" test compares the rest of the piece with the old records put back, as before.
+- **Save, TWT7 body level 4** (header level stays 41: the body level already gates older tw/track builds, as 3c
+  did): a bundle with any track end joined sets its flags' bit 8, and then each track's varint is followed by its
+  joins (`Join::code`: 0 auto, 1 left, 2 right, 3 loose; end a in bits 0-1, b in 2-3); levels 1-3 held single
+  track's joins in flag bits 8-11, read as before. A piece without joins writes the same bytes as at level 3. Keys are
+  not saved (a load gives key = slot). A join a double can't hold yet, a code past 3, or flag bits 9-11 count as
+  unread. Old bodies (TWT4-6) never wrote a loose code; one there counts as unread. `pipeline/readsave.py` reads
+  level 4.
+- Docs: track-and-service.md ("Tracks"), architecture.md section 11, code-map.md (`tracks.rs`).
+
+## Not done (later stages)
+
+- No tool makes a loose end yet (T-4024 Add a track will); no app change, no player text.
+- Joins left/right on a double, explicit ways on a double, three or more tracks: refused (`valid`) until paths name
+  tracks (T-4033). Offsets and purpose are not in the record: nothing sets them, TWT7's fields stay unread.
+- A double's way is still "by the running side" (0 in the record), so the running-side flip needs no rewrite.
+- **For T-4024: an edit that makes a track end loose must route or refuse the lines through it.** Probe
+  (`t4031_a_loose_end_at_a_station_a_line_runs_through`): a station at B, line A-B-C, the eastbound track made loose
+  at B by a plain `Op::Edge` is accepted and leaves the line broken (path cut to its first leg). The route search
+  seeds every leaving end at a stop without asking for a move from the arriving track, so a reroute could find a
+  path `check_line` refuses there too. T-4024's edit should take `way_lines`' shape (reroute through the same stops
+  or refuse naming the line). Loose at a bare end is untested.
+
+## Departures from notes/T-4030.md row a
+
+- `Join` is `Auto`, `Left`, `Right`, `Loose`, not `To(slot across)`: left and right are today's single-track joins
+  and nothing yet joins a track to a slot (stage c, with paths naming tracks).
+- No purpose or offset in `TrackRec`: nothing sets them; TWT7's fields for them stay unread.
+- Joins are saved under the bundle's flag bit 8 (a varint per track), not the reserved node bit 1: a join belongs to
+  a track end, and this keeps a piece without joins at the same bytes.
+- The bracket re-pair rule is not here: a double is always each other's partner; it lands with stage c, where a
+  piece can hold tracks that need it.
