+# T-4032 Runs read the derived edges (T-4030 stage b)
+
+Agent trackruns, 2026-11-22, tree `.tw-trees/trackruns` (branch tw/trackruns from tw/track fdaf5bc2, stages 1-3g and
+4a1; moved onto 4a2, 7f8012e1, and then stage a, ef85f659, before the final checks). Plan: notes/T-4030.md row b and
+sections 1-2; design notes/T-3444-design/05-sim.md section 1 and the parity gates. Advisor consulted once before any
+edit (it set the order, the newtype as the audit, piece-term `build_run`, the sites a cut breaks silently, the id
+range, the twin test with power and the undo check) and once before handing back (it found trains in flight matched
+by derived entry across an edit, fixed below).
+
+## What changed
+
+- **`sim/src/track/derived.rs`** (new): the derived edges runs read. A derived edge is one track's window of its
+  piece's chainage between two derived nodes. `DEntry` (a newtype, `edge << 1 | dir`, `dir` along the piece) has no
+  bit operators and no way in from a raw `u32` outside the file, so every piece-entry decode (`>> 1`, `& 1`, `^ 1`)
+  on a run's entries failed to compile and was rewritten (about 75 sites in 14 files). Accessors on `Network`:
+  `d_entries` (a piece entry to its derived entries in order), `d_pentry`, `d_piece`, `d_track`, `d_window`,
+  `d_len`, `d_nodes`, `d_inner_to` (arrives at a cut, not a piece end), `d_along` / `d_piece_s` (piece chainage to
+  an offset along the entry and back), `d_turns_back`, `d_move_at`, `d_arrive_side`, `d_directed`, `d_of_piece`,
+  `d_slot` / `d_slots`; `Run::pentries` (one piece entry per entry, lined up with `nodes`) and `Run::piece_path`
+  (the path it was built from, a cut track's parts as one).
+- **Identity**: while no track is cut (every save and game today), a track's one derived edge has the track's id,
+  so capacity keys are the track ids they were, and every whole-window reader takes the old expression verbatim
