+## What changed
+
+- **The sim tells the app each entry's track** (`wasm/snapshot.rs`): `line_path_tracks(id)`, per entry of `line_path`,
+  the index of its track among its piece's tracks (`track_rows`' order, which is `ClockEdge.offsets`' order), and
+  `line_back_tracks(id)`, the same per entry of the return run's path as the service runs it (`runs[1].piece_path`:
+  `line_back_path` where that is set, else the path backward, of the part a partly built line runs; empty, as
+  `line_back_path` is, for a line run one way round, a bus or a ferry, whose return is not the path backward). Both are empty
+  where no piece on the path has more than two tracks, so every existing save reads nothing new. `app_entry` and every
+  other export are unchanged. `stateRows` reads them with a line's other heavy parts (`ClockLine.tracks`,
+  `backTracks`, absent when empty).
+- **Ribbons** (`map/network.ts`): on a piece drawn track by track (three or more: `LanePoints.more`, 3d's per-track
+  strokes; `trackLane`), a line's stroke runs along its own track's points, and where its return run is the path
+  backward but on another track (an A B pair), along that track too, drawn as the path's stroke (same band, same
+  direction), appended after the forward strokes like a return leg's. Two tracks of a piece (one lane stroke) are
+  untouched.
+- **Bands** (`map/lineBands.ts`): `BandLine.tracks` (per path entry the track's offset, NaN off such pieces) is the
+  first key of the pairwise order, so lines on different tracks of one piece sit side by side in their tracks' order
+  zoomed out; otherwise the old rule. Its metres to the ribbon's middle are taken from the line's track
+  (`bandPoints`' `track`), so with bands on the ribbons sit exactly where lines sharing the piece would, and fold
+  onto their tracks as the bands go (`bandOn` falls to 0 as double track opens). The band cache's signature and its
+  per-edge fingerprint carry the tracks. Not done: corridors are not fed per-track polylines (tracks 4 m apart fall
+  under `COINCIDE_M`, where ground order is not kept).
+- **Trains**: samples still follow the piece's centre line (`run_polyline`); per sample `sampleTrack` (4 floats:
+  run 0's track offset and run 1's on that piece, m left of run 0, eased at the ends as the stroke is,
+  `offsetAlong` factored out of `trackPoints`; and 1 where the line has a band) and lane 0 there, so no keeping to a
+  side. The train shader adds `trackPx` (true px per metre, less the band's share as bands come on) at the three
+  places it shifts a train; the CPU (`pointAt`, so picking, the inspector and the camera follow) does the same.
+  Texture unit 14, `u_tracks` off and a one-texel texture when no line runs on such a piece; `sampleTrack` in
+  `SAME_FIELDS` (an absent array is never "same", as `samplePass`).
+- Docs: ui-map.md ("Each track at its own offset", "Close in, trains keep to their side", the bands' order).
