+# T-4036 Routing to stop points (track rework stage f)
+
+Agent trackroute, 2026-11-22, tree `.tw-trees/trackroute` (branch tw/trackroute from tw/track 09c90ccd). Plan:
+notes/T-4030.md row f. Advisor consulted before the first edit and before handing back (the second
+time it asked for the reads test, the one-way-leg case taken out and filed, and the claims below made exact). It set the shape: a hop's arrival as an entry, not a
+side (one fix for the anchor seeds, T-4033's seeding and T-3952's first-stop turn); paths stay whole-piece entries
+with one join helper; the goal ranked by the time at the anchor; one "stop nodes of a path" helper for every matcher,
+plain piece nodes where no stop is an anchor; picks on anchors as separate work; twins through the real entry points;
+the order below with parity after each step. It also predicted the `route_of` crash a run ending at an anchor met.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Hops arrive on an entry** (`net/paths.rs` `Arrived`, `find_hop`): a line's hop after the first starts from the
+  previous hop's last entry, leaving by that track end's moves and turning by the node's turn moves (T-3952's table),
+  where before every leaving track on the other side was seeded. `find_path(from, to, side)` keeps the side test
+  (the fingerprint's 600 pairs ask by side). `route_hops_plain_t`, `route_memo` (its `HopMemo` keyed by the arrival),
+  `route_plain_close` and `take_legs` all chain hops this way.
+- **Anchors in the search**: from an anchor a train sets off along its piece either way on every track running so
+  (each priced by `piece_time`, its share of `edge_time` by the speed limits); after arriving (a stop between a line's
+  ends) it carries straight on along its arriving entry, no turn (a cut has no moves). A hop to an anchor ends on its
+  piece's entry: a `Goal` in the heap keyed by the time at the anchor, so arrivals from the two ends rank right; on a
+  seed entry only an anchor ahead counts. The side at an anchor is the direction along its piece (0 a to b).
+  `join_hop` keeps the piece entry once where a hop starts at an anchor; `carry_on_side` and `joined_by` know anchors.
+- **Paths stay whole pieces** (01-model's span). A line ending at an anchor holds its whole end piece: `build_run`
+  trims the run's derived entries there (`stop_nodes_for` trims the matcher's nodes the same way), so its runs start
+  and end at the anchor.
+- **One stop-nodes helper** (`stops.rs` `stop_nodes_for` / `stop_nodes_ends`, `StopNodes` with `arr`, `off`, `pk`,
+  `inner`, `path_from`/`path_to`, `stop_turns`/`path_turns`): where no stop is an anchor it is the piece path's nodes
+  exactly as before (parity by construction); else the anchors are put in and an anchor end trimmed. Read by
+  check_line (an anchor terminus now matches; `check_anchor_stops`), `way_runs`, `stop_ways`, `line_stretch`,
+  `route_legs_t`, `partner_back`'s fit, `order_cost` and `stop_spread` (lengths to the anchor), `edited_stops`'
+  lollipop, `settle_ones`, `dropped`, `stopped_at` (a passed anchor can be put in), `passed_stations`, the loop tools
+  (`branch_end`, `every_pass`, `turn_last`, `turn_first`; `loop_back`'s index mapped by `at`), `path_has_node`.
+- **Related lines** (`wasm/related.rs` `route_of`): the route keeps the run's nodes, anchors among them, and a part
+  of a cut track is an entry of its own keyed by piece and place along it (`PART_BASE`), sampled in its window. Before,
+  a run ending at an anchor indexed past its node offsets (a panic) and a stop at an anchor was never marked.
+- **Picks on anchors** (`perdir.rs`): `way_limited` and `serves_way` read an anchor's platforms by track
+  (`anchor_serves`); `way_runs` decides each run's stop there by whether its own track has a platform. So 4a2's smart
+  allocation works on anchors on double track (a one-track station's pick). One-way legs as anchors (her split) do
+  not: see departures.
+- Docs: track-and-service.md "Tracks" (routing to anchors), code-map.md (`stops.rs`). Test hooks:
+  `TrackApi::of_world`, `world_mut`, `into_world`, `issue_text` (cfg(test)).
+
+## Checks
+
+- **Twins** (`derived_route_tests.rs`, under `derived::tests`; e's pattern: one edit each from equal twins, then
+  `reload`, every run figure and capacity resource to 1e-12 straight, 2e-5 curved, single and double, plus stops,
+  path in piece terms and broken flags): `t4036_terminus_at_anchor_as_split` (two new lines by
+  `set_line_with_trains`, one ending at the station, one starting there; the Platform and Terminus resources there),
