+/// T-3957 (her decision 10, the T-3662 fix): the ways `set` asks for (piece, `TrackRec::way`), each spread along
+/// its track to the nearest branch points (`Network::track_trace`), so a one-way leg never ends up one way part of
+/// the way: turned for each piece walked b to a. A piece asked for keeps its own; of two spreading onto a piece, the
+/// first asked wins. `set` and the result are (piece, slot, way). Without `tracks`, refused (`Tracks`) for a way on
+/// anything but single track, as before; with it (T-4038), any track of a piece but a crossover, a bundle's traced
+/// by its slot (`track_trace` carries slot i on as slot i).
+pub(super) fn spread_ways(net: &crate::track::net::Network, set: &[(u32, u8, u8)], tracks: bool) -> Result<Vec<(u32, u8, u8)>, Issue> {
